From b0c2fed1b2a301b1ad81e33c46cafb3c0efe2e84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 16:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] drm/vc4: reorder of_dma_configure + clear stale xen_swiotlb_dma_ops

A `dma_set_mask -EIO` WARN persisted, and pinpointing the root cause to
line 832 shows that a simple reorder is not enough:

  kernel/dma/mapping.c line 828-834:
    static int dma_supported(struct device *dev, u64 mask)
    {
        const struct dma_map_ops *ops = get_dma_ops(dev);
        if (use_dma_iommu(dev)) {
            if (WARN_ON(ops))           <- line 832
                return false;
            return true;
        }
        ...

The WARN fires on the contradiction `dev->dma_iommu == true` together with
`dev->dma_ops != NULL`.

Tracing dev->dma_ops through
arch/arm64/mm/dma-mapping.c::arch_setup_dma_ops shows that at platform
device alloc time it calls xen_setup_dma_ops(), and under Xen Dom0
xen_swiotlb_detect() == true so dev->dma_ops = &xen_swiotlb_dma_ops is set
(include/xen/arm/xen-ops.h).

axi:gpu (a reg-less container node) skips of_dma_configure at
platform_device_alloc time, so the switch to IOMMU mode never runs and it
reaches vc4_drm_bind with dev->dma_iommu = false. There the vc4 driver
calls of_dma_configure(hvs_node, true) to set dev->dma_iommu = true, but
xen_swiotlb_dma_ops is not cleared, so the contradiction triggers the WARN
and -EIO.

On bare-metal RPi5 xen_swiotlb_detect() == false, so dev->dma_ops stays
NULL, there is no contradiction, and vc4-drm bind succeeds.

Fix:
1. Move of_dma_configure before dma_set_mask_and_coherent (sets
   dev->dma_iommu = true and allocates dev->dma_mask).
2. Also clear the xen_swiotlb direct-ops residue with
   `if (dev->dma_iommu) dev->dma_ops = NULL` after of_dma_configure.

This lets dma_supported() pass without the WARN under Xen Dom0.

Side-effect assessment:
- bare-metal: dev->dma_iommu stays false, so the if-guard skips the clear;
  no effect.
- Xen DomU passthrough: dev->dma_iommu = false (via xen_swiotlb); no
  effect.
- other drivers: change is confined to the vc4 driver.
- IOMMU functionality: of_dma_configure still enters iommu mode correctly,
  so functionality is preserved.

Refer: include/xen/arm/xen-ops.h::xen_setup_dma_ops()
Refer: kernel/dma/mapping.c::dma_supported() line 828-834

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-4-8
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_drv.c | 50 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 44 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_drv.c
@@ -332,11 +332,37 @@
 	else
 		driver = &vc4_drm_driver;
 
-	if (gen >= VC4_GEN_6_C)
-		dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(36));
-	else
-		dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32));
-
+	/*
+	 * Handle xen_swiotlb_dma_ops
+	 * residue + reorder of_dma_configure before dma_set_mask.
+	 *
+	 * The vc4 aggregate device (`/axi/gpu`) is a container DT node with no
+	 * `reg` property, so platform_device_alloc() does not call
+	 * of_dma_configure() for it. We must do it manually, otherwise
+	 * dev->dma_mask is NULL and dev->iommu is uninitialized, and
+	 * dma_set_mask() returns -EIO.
+	 *
+	 * Under Xen Dom0 there is an additional twist: arch_setup_dma_ops()
+	 * unconditionally calls xen_setup_dma_ops() (arch/arm64/mm/dma-mapping.c),
+	 * which sets `dev->dma_ops = &xen_swiotlb_dma_ops` whenever
+	 * xen_swiotlb_detect() is true. That happens BEFORE any device-specific
+	 * setup, so axi:gpu lands at vc4_drm_bind() with both:
+	 *   - dev->dma_ops    == &xen_swiotlb_dma_ops  (set by xen_setup_dma_ops)
+	 *   - dev->dma_iommu  == false                  (not yet configured)
+	 *
+	 * After of_dma_configure() below switches the device to IOMMU mode
+	 * (dev->dma_iommu = true), dma_supported() inside dma_set_mask()
+	 * detects both flags set and triggers WARN_ON(ops) at mapping.c:832 —
+	 * that's an assertion against the iommu/direct-ops contradiction. We
+	 * have to clear dev->dma_ops manually because xen_setup_dma_ops()
+	 * doesn't reconcile with later iommu setup.
+	 *
+	 * On bare-metal RPi5 xen_swiotlb_detect() returns false so
+	 * dev->dma_ops stays NULL and the WARN never fires.
+	 *
+	 * An earlier variant that only set the mask still hit
+	 * WARN_ON(ops) at dma_supported().
+	 */
 	node = of_find_matching_node_and_match(NULL, vc4_dma_range_matches,
 					       NULL);
 	if (node) {
@@ -347,6 +373,19 @@
 			return ret;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Reconcile with xen_setup_dma_ops(): IOMMU mode is mutually exclusive
+	 * with direct dma_ops. Without this clear, dma_supported() bails out
+	 * with WARN_ON(ops != NULL) for Xen Dom0 builds.
+	 */
+	if (dev->dma_iommu)
+		dev->dma_ops = NULL;
+
+	if (gen >= VC4_GEN_6_C)
+		dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(36));
+	else
+		dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32));
+
 	vc4 = devm_drm_dev_alloc(dev, driver, struct vc4_dev, base);
 	if (IS_ERR(vc4))
 		return PTR_ERR(vc4);
